  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

  <h3>Will I lose quality when converting MP3 to WAV?</h3>
  <p>No — no additional quality is lost. The original MP3 compression cannot be undone, but the resulting WAV file is stored losslessly from that point on.</p>

  <h3>How large will the WAV file be?</h3>
  <p>A 3-minute WAV file (44.1 kHz, 16-bit, stereo) is about 30 MB — compared to around 3–7 MB as MP3. Plan your storage accordingly.</p>

